          "description": {
            "comment": "Ustilago bromivora is a biotrophic pathogenic fungus belonging to the group of head smuts. It infects the model grass Brachypodium distachyon and causes visible symptoms in the late stages of the plant development were infected spikelets are converted to smut sori. The well-established model smut fungus Ustilago maydis has been previously shown to be a useful to study aspects of biotrophic pathogenic fungi in general.",
